BCC_Q({"y": 2025, "n": 13, "part": "C", "topic": "logic", "title": "Apple Classification", "answer": 2, "story": "<p>At Beaver Orchard, a machine sorts apples into eight weight-based\ngrades, with apples of the same grade sent to the same packaging\narea.<\/p>\n<p>Apples are fed into the top of the machine, move through different\nchutes, and land in one of 8 bins at the bottom of the machine. As each\napple moves through the machine, it passes weight sensors that determine\nits path through the chutes. If the weight of an apple is greater than\nor equal to the sensor's value, then the apple will drop through the\nright chute; otherwise, it will drop through the left chute.<\/p>\n<p>For example, the given diagram shows the result when apples of\nweights 9, 12, and 13 pass through a sensor of value 12. The apple of\nweight 9 will drop through the left chute, while the apples of weights\n12 and 13 will drop through the right chute.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:1.78889in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<p>The machine has already sorted some apples and the results are shown\nin the following diagram. The displays on the weight sensors labelled X,\nY, and Z are broken and so do not show these sensors' values.<\/p>\n<div class=\"center\">\n<p> <img alt=\"The machine has 7 sensors: 1 on the top level, 2 in the middle level, and 4 in the bottom level. There is a right chute and a left chute from each sensor and a bin below each chute from the bottom level sensors. Apples with weights ranging from 1 to 20 are in the eight bins. A complete description of the machine follows.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:7.25556in\"/> <\/p>\n<\/div>\n<button onclick=\"hideSeek('longdesc0')\" style=\"box-shadow: none;\">Hide/Reveal Description of Diagram for Apple Classification<\/button>\n<div id=\"longdesc0\" style=\"display: none;\">\n<ul>\n<li>Top level: Sensor X.<\/li>\n<li>Middle level: From sensor X, the right chute leads to a sensor with value 16 and the left chute leads to sensor Y.<\/li>\n<li>Bottom level: \n<ul>\n<li>From sensor 16, the right chute leads to sensor Z and the left chute leads to a sensor with value 14.\n<ul>\n<li>From sensor Z, weight 20 went right and weights 17 and 18 went left.<\/li>\n<li>From sensor 14, weights 14 and 15 went right and weights 12 and 13 went left.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<li>From sensor Y, the right chute leads to a sensor with value 9 and the left chute leads to a sensor with value 4.\n<ul>\n<li>From sensor 9, weight 9 went right and weight 8 went left.<\/li>\n<li>From sensor 4, weight 5 went right and weights 1 and 3 went left.<\/li>\n<\/ul><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<hr class=\"longdesc\"/><\/div>", "question": "<p>Which of the following are possible values for the weight sensors\nlabelled X, Y, and Z?<\/p>\n<ol class=\"mc\">\n<li> <img alt=\"X with value 10, Y with value 5, and Z with value 18.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.08333in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<li> <img alt=\"X with value 11, Y with value 6, and Z with value 17.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.08333in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<li> <img alt=\"X with value 12, Y with value 7, and Z with value 20.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.08333in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<li> <img alt=\"X with value 13, Y with value 8, and Z with value 19.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.08333in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/li>\n<\/ol>", "answerHtml": "<p>(C) <img alt=\"X with value 12, Y with value 7, and Z with value 20.\" class=\"static\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" style=\"width:2.08333in; vertical-align:middle;\"/> <\/p>", "explanation": "<p>First we look at the sensor labelled X. Of the apples that dropped\nthrough the left chute at this sensor, the heaviest weight was 9. Of the\napples that dropped through the right chute, the lightest weight was 12.\nThus, X can be 10, 11, or 12. From this, we can exclude Option D.<\/p>\n<p>Next we look at the sensor labelled Y. Of the apples that dropped\nthrough the left chute at this sensor, the heaviest weight was 5. Of the\napples that dropped through the right chute, the lightest weight was 8.\nThus, Y can be 6, 7, or 8. From this, we can exclude Option A.<\/p>\n<p>Finally we look at the sensor labelled Z. Of the apples that dropped\nthrough the left chute at this sensor, the heaviest weight was 18. The\nonly apple that that dropped through the right chute had a weight of 20.\nThus, Z can be 19 or 20. From this, we can exclude Option B.<\/p>\n<p>Thus, the only option that shows possible values for all three\nsensors is Option C, as it satisfies all the conditions.<\/p>", "connections": "", "mc": 1});